.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-NETPLAN 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-netplan
.Nd show and check the address ranges kldload uses for its own networks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm show
.Nm
.Cm get
.Ar key
.Nm
.Cm check
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
kldload runs networks of its own: the Kubernetes pod and service ranges,
the network its cluster machines sit on, WireGuard meshes, lab networks
and libvirt networks.
Their ranges are listed in one place, the network plan, and
.Nm
prints it and checks it.
.Pp
The plan is read from
.Pa /usr/lib/kldload/network-plan.defaults ,
then
.Pa /etc/kldload/network-plan.env ,
whose lines replace the defaults' key by key.
Both hold
.Ar KEY Ns = Ns Ar range
lines, where a range is an address, a CIDR block or two addresses joined
by
.Ql - ;
.Ql #
starts a comment.
The files are parsed, never run as shell.
A line of any other shape is ignored, and
.Cm check
names it.
.Pp
The keys and what uses them are described in the defaults file itself.
.Ql NET_BLOCK
is the block every kldload network is meant to move into; until they have,
.Cm check
lists those outside it without calling it a problem.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm show
Print every key and its range, one per line, in the order the files give
them.
.It Cm get Ar key
Print the range for
.Ar key
alone, for use in scripts.
.It Cm check
Report, one line each:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
a line in either file that is not a
.Ar KEY Ns = Ns Ar range ;
.It
a value that is not an address, a range or a CIDR block;
.It
any two of the plan's networks that overlap;
.It
.Ql K8S_VIP
or
.Ql K8S_LB_POOL
outside
.Ql K8S_NODE_NET ,
or the VIP inside the pool;
.It
a network of the plan that overlaps a route this host has through an
interface kldload does not own \(em a LAN on a bridge or a NIC, a VPN.
Interfaces named
.Ql virbr* , kld-* , wg* , cilium_* , lxc* , vnet* , tap*
and
.Ql fc-*
are kldload's or libvirt's, and are not compared.
.El
.Pp
Each problem is a
.Ql FAIL
line; the last line counts ranges and problems.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev NETPLAN_DEFAULTS
Read the defaults from this file instead.
.It Ev NETPLAN_FILE
Read the overrides from this file instead: how to try a change before
making it.
.It Ev NETPLAN_ROUTES
Check against the routes in this file, in the form
.Ql ip -4 route show
prints, instead of this host's.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /usr/lib/kldload/network-plan.defaults
The plan as kldload ships it.
.It Pa /etc/kldload/network-plan.env
This host's changes to it.
.It Pa /usr/lib/kldload/netplan.sh
The reader every kldload tool that uses the plan sources.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Done;
.Cm check
found nothing.
.It 1
.Cm check
found a problem, or
.Cm get
was given a key the plan does not have.
.It 2
A usage error.
.It 3
Neither plan file could be read.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed by
.Nm
on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-29, whose LAN,
.Ql 10.100.10.0/24 ,
is on
.Ql br0 .
.Ss The plan (show)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kldload-netplan show
NET_BLOCK            10.240.0.0/12
K8S_POD_CIDR         10.244.0.0/16
K8S_SVC_CIDR         10.96.0.0/16
K8S_NODE_NET         192.168.122.0/24
K8S_VIP              192.168.122.240
K8S_LB_POOL          192.168.122.200-192.168.122.220
WG_MGMT_NET          10.250.0.0/24
WG_K8S_NET           10.251.0.0/24
KLAB_BLUE_NET        10.252.0.0/24
KLAB_GREEN_NET       10.253.0.0/24
KVM_MESH_BLOCK       10.254.0.0/16
PLANE_WG0_NET        10.77.0.0/16
PLANE_WG1_NET        10.78.0.0/16
PLANE_WG2_NET        10.79.0.0/16
PLANE_WG3_NET        10.80.0.0/16
MASTER_CLUSTER_CIDR  10.78.0.0/20
VMNET_KLAB           192.168.150.0/24
VMNET_ZFSLAB         192.168.151.0/24
VMNET_VMS            192.168.152.0/24
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Ss One range (get)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kldload-netplan get K8S_SVC_CIDR
10.96.0.0/16
# (exited 0)
$ echo "services are $(kldload-netplan get K8S_SVC_CIDR)"
services are 10.96.0.0/16
$ kldload-netplan get NO_SUCH_KEY
kldload-netplan: no key NO_SUCH_KEY in the plan
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Ss The shipped plan checked (check)
It carries one known overlap, reported until it is moved:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kldload-netplan check
  FAIL  PLANE_WG1_NET 10.78.0.0/16 overlaps MASTER_CLUSTER_CIDR 10.78.0.0/20
  INFO  checked against 1 route(s) through interfaces kldload does not own
  INFO  outside 10.240.0.0/12 (moved in phase 2 and 3 of docs/NETWORK-PLAN.md): K8S_SVC_CIDR K8S_NODE_NET PLANE_WG0_NET PLANE_WG1_NET PLANE_WG2_NET PLANE_WG3_NET MASTER_CLUSTER_CIDR VMNET_KLAB VMNET_ZFSLAB VMNET_VMS
netplan: 19 ranges, 1 problem(s)
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Ss Trying a change first (NETPLAN_FILE)
This file puts the service range back to the
.Ql /12
it had before 2026-09-29, moves the VIP, and has a line that is not a
setting:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ cat override.env
K8S_SVC_CIDR=10.96.0.0/12
K8S_VIP=10.0.0.5
this is not a line
$ NETPLAN_FILE=override.env kldload-netplan check
  FAIL  not a KEY=range line, ignored: override.env:3: this is not a line
  FAIL  PLANE_WG1_NET 10.78.0.0/16 overlaps MASTER_CLUSTER_CIDR 10.78.0.0/20
  FAIL  K8S_VIP 10.0.0.5 is not inside K8S_NODE_NET 192.168.122.0/24
  FAIL  K8S_SVC_CIDR 10.96.0.0/12 overlaps 10.100.10.0/24, which this host reaches via br0 -- not a kldload network
  INFO  checked against 1 route(s) through interfaces kldload does not own
\&...
netplan: 19 ranges, 4 problem(s)
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Ss Another host's routes (NETPLAN_ROUTES)
A route through
.Ql wg-mgmt
is kldload's own and is not compared; one through
.Ql eth1
is:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ cat routes.txt
10.244.8.0/22 dev eth1 proto kernel scope link src 10.244.8.1
10.250.0.0/24 dev wg-mgmt proto kernel scope link src 10.250.0.1
$ NETPLAN_ROUTES=routes.txt kldload-netplan check
  FAIL  PLANE_WG1_NET 10.78.0.0/16 overlaps MASTER_CLUSTER_CIDR 10.78.0.0/20
  FAIL  K8S_POD_CIDR 10.244.0.0/16 overlaps 10.244.8.0/22, which this host reaches via eth1 -- not a kldload network
  INFO  checked against 1 route(s) through interfaces kldload does not own
\&...
netplan: 19 ranges, 2 problem(s)
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Ss No plan (NETPLAN_DEFAULTS)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ NETPLAN_DEFAULTS=/nonexistent kldload-netplan show
kldload-netplan: no plan file (/nonexistent)
# (exited 3)
.Ed
.Ss Usage (-h, --help)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kldload-netplan --help
kldload-netplan — show and check the ranges kldload uses for its own networks.

  kldload-netplan show        every range, one per line: KEY VALUE
  kldload-netplan get KEY     one value (for scripts)
  kldload-netplan check       exit 1 if any two kldload ranges overlap, if
                              the VIP or MetalLB pool falls outside its node
                              network, or if a range overlaps a route this
                              host reaches through an interface kldload does
                              not own (a LAN on br0, eth0, ...)

.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "FAIL  A RANGE overlaps B RANGE"
Two of kldload's networks share addresses; traffic for one can be routed
to the other.
.It "FAIL  KEY RANGE overlaps DEST, which this host reaches via DEV -- not a kldload network"
A kldload network covers addresses of a network this host is really on:
the machines there become unreachable from anything that routes the
kldload range.
.It "FAIL  not a KEY=range line, ignored: FILE:LINE: TEXT"
The line was skipped; the default for that key stands.
.It "kldload-netplan: no plan file (PATH)"
Neither file could be read; tools that use the plan fall back to the
ranges they carried before it existed.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ip-route 8 ,
.Xr kube-cluster 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
was written on 2026-09-29, the day the Kubernetes service range,
.Ql 10.96.0.0/12 ,
was found to contain the bench LAN
.Ql 10.100.10.0/24
with nothing able to say so.
The service range is
.Ql 10.96.0.0/16
since.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Not every tool reads the plan yet; some still carry their ranges as
literals.
Changing a range here moves only the tools that read it, and a range that
is in use \(em a running cluster's pod range \(em does not move with it.
.Pp
Only IPv4 is planned and checked.
